{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"releases-and-upgrading","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Releases and upgrading"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"today","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Today"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every package is at "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"0.3.1"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on npm, released together. Every\nrelease and what came with it is on the "},{"type":"link","href":"/changelog","children":[{"type":"text","value":"changelog"}]},{"type":"text","value":", read from\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"CHANGELOG.md","source":"CHANGELOG.md"}},{"type":"text","value":" in the repository."}]},{"type":"component","name":"packages","attributes":{},"children":[]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-versions-work","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How versions work"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One version for everything."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The compiler, the adapters, the CLI, the language\nserver and the packages release together at the same number. A diagnostic touches\nthe engine, the lint rules, the editor and the documentation at once, so a version\nwhere those disagree would be a version that lies."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before 1.0, the API can move."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A minor version may change behaviour; a patch\nonly fixes. Every such change gets an entry in the release notes saying what\nmoved and what to do."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After 1.0"}]},{"type":"text","value":", semantic versioning: a breaking change means a major."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-counts-as-breaking","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What counts as breaking"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removing or renaming an export, or changing what it returns."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changing which style wins: the ladder, merge semantics, layer order."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changing a diagnostic's meaning. (Codes and names are stable once released;\na code may gain a better message, never a different subject.)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changing generated class names in a way that breaks a shared page, other than\nthrough the configured prefix."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What is "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" breaking: new diagnostics, new API, better messages, smaller output."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-you-upgrade","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you upgrade"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the release note for behaviour changes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> check","source":"kirana-style check"}},{"type":"text","value":": new diagnostics surface here first, and a new warning is\nusually a real problem that was invisible before."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build, and diff the stylesheet. Output is deterministic, so a diff is\nmeaningful: it shows exactly which declarations changed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the project has a visual baseline, compare computed styles rather than\nscreenshots. "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/advanced/conformance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Conformance"}]},{"type":"text","value":" explains the method."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"releases-and-upgrading","text":"Releases and upgrading","level":1},{"id":"today","text":"Today","level":2},{"id":"how-versions-work","text":"How versions work","level":2},{"id":"what-counts-as-breaking","text":"What counts as breaking","level":2},{"id":"when-you-upgrade","text":"When you upgrade","level":2}]}
